module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.DifferentialGraded.RightModule.DerivedHomReflectorExists

/-!
# Steps 1 and 2 of Tag 09LK, with the reflector's data kept

`DGCategory.exists_isTriangulated_derivedHomReflector` packages steps 1 and 2 of the replacement
proof of [Stacks, Tag 09LK] as the existence of an exact `R̃ : D(A) ⥤ D(E)` together with a unit
and a `Nonempty` comparison `q ⋙ R̃ ≅ Φ ⋙ L ⋙ ev_K ⋙ Q_E`. That shape is enough for the
*statement* of step 2, but it is not enough for step 3: the identification `(*)` that step 3
consumes is a map out of `H^n(U(R̃(q X)))`, and the only construction of such a map available is
the chain `DGCategory.RightModule.chainEquivReflectorEvaluation`, which is a bijection out of
`H^n(ev_K (L (Φ X)))` and whose hypotheses are

* `hL`: every `L X` is local for the localizing subcategory `N` generated by the representables,
  and
* `hη`: the cone of every `η.app X` lies in `N`.

Both are discarded by `DGCategory.exists_isTriangulated_derivedHomReflector`, which keeps only
`L`'s exactness and the existence of the comparison; and the comparison it produces is bound by
`Nonempty`, so the relation of the unit it returns to the reflector is discarded too. A proof of
`(*)` that started from that statement would have to *reconstruct* `hL` and `hη` for the `L` it
was handed — which it cannot, since `L` is bound by an existential — or invoke step 1 a second
time and then identify two unrelated reflectors.

This file records the data-preserving form: the reflector, its unit and the three hypotheses
`hL`, `hη` and `hΦ`, with nothing about `R̃` in the statement. At those data `R̃` and its unit are
*definitionally* `DGCategory.derivedHomReflector` and `DGCategory.derivedHomReflectorUnit`, so
every lemma about them — the comparison
`DGCategory.derivedHomReflectorCompIso`, the source identification
`DGCategory.derivedHomReflectorGradedCohomologyIso`, and the chain with the same `hL` and `hη` —
applies to the same objects, and no witness has to be identified with another.

## Main results

* `DGCategory.exists_derivedHomReflector_data`: **steps 1 and 2 with their data kept.** The
  reflector, its unit, the locality of its values, the hypothesis on the cones of its unit, and
  the vanishing of `L ∘ Φ` on `Z`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09LK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09LK)
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace DGCategory

universe v₂ u₂ v₁ u₁ v r

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated
open CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty

variable {R : Type r} [CommRing R] (C : DGCategory.{v, v} R) {ι : Type v} (G : ι → C.Obj)
  {S : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} S] [HasZeroObject S] [HasShift S ℤ] [Preadditive S]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor S n).Additive] [Pretriangulated S] [IsTriangulated S]
  (Φ : S ⥤ (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K) [Φ.CommShift ℤ] [Φ.IsTriangulated]
  (Z : ObjectProperty S) [Z.IsTriangulated]

omit [HasZeroObject S] [HasShift S ℤ] [Preadditive S] [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor S n).Additive]
  [Pretriangulated S] [IsTriangulated S] [Φ.CommShift ℤ] [Φ.IsTriangulated] [Z.IsTriangulated] in
/-- **Steps 1 and 2 of [Stacks, Tag 09LK], with the reflector's data kept.** Let `Φ` carry every
object of the triangulated subcategory `Z` into the localizing subcategory `N` of
`K(Mod^dg(C))` generated by the representables `h_{G i}`. Then there are an exact reflector `L`
onto the `N`-local objects and a unit `η : 𝟭 ⟶ L` such that

* every `L X` is `N`-local,
* the cone of every `η.app X` lies in `N`, and
* `L (Φ X)` is zero for every object `X` of `Z`.

The last clause is the hypothesis `hΦ` of `DGCategory.derivedHomReflector`, so at these data the
exact functor `R̃ : D(A) ⥤ D(E)` of step 2 and its unit are the named
`DGCategory.derivedHomReflector` and `DGCategory.derivedHomReflectorUnit`, rather than witnesses
of an existential; and the first two clauses are the hypotheses `hL` and `hη` of
`DGCategory.RightModule.chainEquivReflectorEvaluation`, so the chain is available at the *same*
reflector and unit.

Compared with `DGCategory.exists_isTriangulated_derivedHomReflector` nothing is strengthened:
the three clauses are the three conclusions of step 1,
`DGCategory.RightModule.exists_isTriangulated_reflector_yonedaObjK_of_dgCategory`, the third
being derived from the first two exactly as that theorem's proof derives it. What changes is only
that they are not thrown away. -/
theorem exists_derivedHomReflector_data
    (hZ : ∀ X, Z X → RightModule.yonedaLocalizing C G (Φ.obj X)) :
    ∃ (L : (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K ⥤ (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K)
      (_ : L.CommShift ℤ) (_ : L.IsTriangulated) (η : 𝟭 _ ⟶ L)
      (_ : ∀ X, (RightModule.yonedaLocalizing C G).rightOrthogonal (L.obj X))
      (_ : ∀ (X Y : (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K) (f : Y ⟶ X)
          (g : L.obj X ⟶ Y⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧),
        Triangle.mk f (η.app X) g ∈ distTriang (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K →
          RightModule.yonedaLocalizing C G Y),
      ∀ X, Z X → IsZero ((Φ ⋙ L).obj X) := by
  obtain ⟨L, cs, tri, η, h₁, h₂, h₃⟩ :=
    RightModule.exists_isTriangulated_reflector_yonedaObjK_of_dgCategory C G
  exact ⟨L, cs, tri, η, h₁, h₃, fun X hX =>
    isZero_of_bijective_precomp_unit _ (h₁ (Φ.obj X)) (h₂ _ (h₁ (Φ.obj X)) (Φ.obj X)).1
      (hZ X hX)⟩

end DGCategory

end
